   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Food preferences and politeness",
     "texto": [
      "To say you like something, Dutch does not use a verb like English «like». Instead it uses «lekker vinden» (literally «to find tasty»): «Ik vind de soep lekker» (I like the soup). In questions: «Vindt u de soep lekker?» (Do you like the soup?). To order politely in a restaurant, use «Ik wil graag...» (I would like...): «Ik wil graag soep»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
